{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Upon me</b> — Because he likened himself to the depths of the sea, for he is banished from the dry land in the wrath of HaShem, therefore <b>upon me</b> Your wrath leans, in the manner of <b>ki Shaddai's arrows are with me</b> (Job 6:4), whose wrath drinks my spirit." "And the word <b>upon me</b> — serves in place of another, and <b>all Your breakers</b> — <b>You have borne</b> upon me, selah." "<b>And You have borne</b> — like <b>nations roar</b> (Psalms 46:3)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 88, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:19.323312780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}